{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1484820824,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDE4MTYxMTE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1200","origin":"github"},"title":"Better exception(s) for paths outside of a repo","message":"We already have `PathOutsideRepositoryError`, which is to be thrown if a repo was asked to operate on a path outside of its scope. Therefore this exception currently expects a repo to be specified.\nIn `Interface._prep()` (`datalad/interface/base.py`) we also need a very similar exception without a specific repository. Additionally such an exception needs to be able to properly deal with reporting multiple paths. We should either make `PathOutsideRepositoryError` more general or have base exception for it in order to not have several not related exceptions, which basically indicate the same thing.","files":null}]}